{"2791263553":"Staff collect children at dismissal and walk or drive them to the program.","721ce1406c":"School’s out. Now what?","b4ea78edb2":"Find the after-school programs that work with your child’s school: what runs in the building, who picks up at dismissal, and what’s close enough to walk to.","4b844d0798":"Find your school or a program","9f6c7e2886":"Every district and charter school in the city is in here. If yours isn’t covered yet, you can ask for it.","65a1412e26":"Weekend classes","926f053689":"Saturday and Sunday classes at {n} places: music, dance, art, skating, science.","242e0d11b4":"Day camps","189c3fbfde":"{n} programs run camps on the days school is closed, with a planner for the year.","4f19f8d878":"Summer camps","ab0c648ef7":"{n} day camps in the city, with ages, hours and prices, and a schedule to plan the summer week by week.","8a300b908c":"Days off this year, and who’s open","54acc2806d":"Start here","280cfd1a5b":"Parents","5a85ffc912":"See what works with your child’s school, then put the week together.","77687dbe0c":"Find your school","93c7200926":"Every program that’s there, picks up or is nearby","111a61cb3d":"Build a schedule","6bd96c1814":"A week of programs, and a card to send","65e5b31cc6":"Create a free account","54905fb796":"Keep your school and week on every device","4ab2910209":"Your account","282c9b433c":"Your school, your week and who you share it with","57597b2c79":"Program managers","0bda3e6531":"Run an after-school program, a weekend class or a camp? Make sure parents see it right.","7c065c3438":"Claim your listing","a79a2ac220":"Keep its dates, costs and hours current yourself","ac858ab685":"Add a program","5f3a66b696":"Not listed yet? Send its name and website","795578f306":"Add a camp","f48fe74ae9":"Summer camps and camps on days off","f8f2f6286e":"Or start somewhere else","757c81f1d0":"By program type","3a62dafeaf":"Music, art, sports, plain old aftercare.","8ed176874c":"By neighborhood","754d6bda83":"What’s based near home, and who comes to pick up.","ee9aa9711a":"All neighborhoods","d4678aa638":"By grade","eea904e13c":"Everything that takes your child’s grade.","b38ad3dcbe":"More than weekday afternoons","89cecd25b9":"After school is where this started. The same listings now cover the rest of a family’s calendar.","d0c8141344":"Have a look","adcb071d03":"Schools covered so far","0898b0b426":"All schools","57c574f80d":"Schools are added one at a time, because every pickup list has to be checked. Search for yours above and ask for it: the ones parents ask for most go first.","6b2d53d0b0":"Get the dates by email","613a8374d0":"Sign-up openings, deadlines and days off for your school, so none of them sneaks up on you.","cd5afd9aa8":"Your school","bfe862f18f":"A school that isn’t listed yet","8ee9829c7e":"Your first name","3fa6f5fb50":"Your email","52554ec612":"Send me the dates","72ba038ef1":"One email on {day} morning, and only in a week with a date coming up. Every email has an unsubscribe link.","c5f1d682cf":"How we handle your email.","55de746305":"Signing up needs JavaScript.","a7d376eed1":"How programs are sorted","19a9b8c07a":"At the school","b78b2d867a":"Runs in the school building or on its grounds. No travel.","c5898fc305":"Picks up","f1536c3517":"Nearby","abbbbdb7e3":"Close to the school, with no pickup we could find. A fit for older children or a second stop.","4ec0a4ca4b":"Every listing is dated and sourced","1a2e23c6b6":"Every listing links to where the information came from and shows the day it was last checked. Nobody pays to be listed. If it saved you an evening of open tabs,","02738a9126":"buy me a coffee.","24463c5f78":"Who built this","a82882c04a":"Josh Silverbauer is a parent of two, with one in the Nebinger catchment. Navigating after-school programs was chaos for him, so he figured it was chaos for everyone else too. His wife Rachael told him to stop complaining and build something. So he built this.","2ded0fc514":"After-school programs in Philadelphia, sorted by the school your child goes to.","e877ba88ef":"Free, and run by one parent.","06c76a46e4":"Schools","6c51011791":"Ask for your school","ab14d0a7db":"Programs","b8741ed7c0":"All programs, A to Z","3e6c889cad":"Programs by type","3a356e1883":"Programs by neighborhood","fb556467b7":"Day-camp programs","0d1fc1aeaa":"Suggest a program","d2684e6248":"Write a review","928655b7f0":"Your family","55cf06857b":"After-school schedule","ef8a7dc9b4":"Day-camp schedule","d4819c397f":"Dates by email","6b21fb791a":"About","5e461a2404":"About this site","5b2fc57ac3":"How listings are checked","1862eb688d":"Send a correction","4832e45812":"Contact us","c192560a97":"For program managers","29c269f6e8":"Request a feature","cf01481f62":"Privacy","8a069ed1c6":"Terms of use","fd1482eac6":"Buy me a coffee","b7e5078568":"Listings come from each provider’s public pages and are not endorsements. Prices, hours and pickup routes change, so confirm with the provider before you enroll.","ab9dba162b":"{site} is an independent community project. It is not affiliated with the School District of Philadelphia or any provider listed.","1ec7041a18":"Questions?","1758356db2":"or","fa1e614bfa":"send a message","c6a087c2ce":"Runs at the school","fe7f975890":"No travel. Children stay in the building or on school grounds.","b94124d4a9":"Picks up from {s}","29124123b4":"Nearby, no pickup found","e6debee5af":"Close to the school, but you or your child would need to get there. Best suited to older children or as a second stop.","7a2b58b28c":"It’s {time} at {school}. Now what?","3efde1b3d3":"Every after-school program we could find that runs at the school, picks children up from {school}, or sits within a short walk. Pick a grade to see what your child can join.","82909c56bf":"Looking for a particular program?","40d1d6bf3c":"Places are put on the map from their street address. The map’s pictures come from OpenStreetMap.","1062db6083":"What that means for your privacy.","bc2762bf17":"The number under each grade counts programs at the school or with pickup.","883a11e036":"Nothing matches that. Know a program that should be listed?","c85d669959":"Tell us about it.","340a874bce":"Can’t decide? Let a theme pick for you.","0eccefea65":"Roll a themed week for {school}","4e3deb80a9":"Know a program that serves {school} and isn’t here?","ec70686841":"Add it to the list.","620043a25b":"Get {school} dates by email","b7f02548f1":"Sign-up openings and deadlines for these programs, and a heads-up before each day off.","1b2b3b5f17":"Checked, and not listing {school} pickup","db866c0163":"Before you enroll","781d95fb05":"Pickup lists change every year, and most providers need a minimum number of children from a school. Ask each one to confirm {school} pickup for the days you need.","d833eb791a":"Ask what happens on early-dismissal days and district days off.","a40b144f44":"City rec centers post each year’s after-school listing late, so call before counting on a price or a spot. Their listings live in the","3a73f7ec9b":"Parks & Rec finder","1e007536e7":"Free, city-funded programs are in the city’s","b0c40867ce":"After School and Summer Program Locator","72e38f81e9":"dismissal","2f364f8eaa":"Search for any district or charter school in Philadelphia. The ones below already have a page; the rest you can ask for.","851df1e67a":"Covered so far","776487435b":"Schools are added one at a time, because every pickup list has to be checked. The ones parents ask for most go first.","3a7d669610":"Not covered yet","d4e6ee0fa9":"Each of these has a page showing what’s close to it, where you can ask for it and be told when it’s added.","e936b4be24":"This school isn’t covered yet","9efecb6136":"Search for your school to see whether it has a page.","95bb52faf1":"Want it added?","add5ed2b5e":"Each school takes real checking, so the ones parents ask for most go first. One tap adds your vote.","b583ab5fc8":"Get an email when it’s added","479ab840e8":"Email me when it’s added","09eff95b4e":"One email when this school gets its page. It also adds you to our email list, for occasional news about the site. Every email has an unsubscribe link.","82d20edb64":"In the meantime","fa9e43a824":"Browse by neighborhood","982d5244f7":"All programs","0bf23c079f":"Know which programs pick up from this school?","b0863e8ad5":"Tell us, and it gets covered faster.","3104cab419":"Look up a school","7176983e9a":"School name","ef4c661463":"This page needs JavaScript. You can also ask for a school with the suggestion form.","d6408faac2":"After school near {school}","dd998a412f":"We haven’t checked which programs pick up from this school yet. Here is what’s close, and how to ask for it to be covered.","1fb4b5cbc4":"Want {school} added?","cb26ac9895":"After-school programs within a mile","077a19c31f":"Nothing we list is within a mile of {school} yet.","4ddfa9043a":"Tell us about a program near it.","a3acb75895":"No school with a page is close by yet. You can still browse by neighborhood or look through every program.","6b7144b80c":"Look up another school","eaf88de8a1":"These are close to {school}, in a straight line. We don’t know yet whether any of them pick up from it, so ask the program.","1abc5cfcb2":"Weekend classes within two miles","c6f503176e":"Saturday and Sunday classes take children from any school.","e64f3f0f22":"All weekend classes","f5e81e462e":"Summer camps within two miles","d558a9fcea":"All summer camps","ac49e85c8c":"The closest school with a page is {name}, about {miles} away. Programs that serve it may reach {school} too, but ask each one.","adc8cf0be9":"After school, by what they do","898f345800":"Pick the kind of program you’re after. Each list can be narrowed by grade and neighborhood.","b8dd50250a":"A program can sit in more than one group: a rec center is also aftercare, and a school’s clubs may include music and chess.","30c8a0fc9c":"All types","a3b1c7d062":"{type}: after-school programs","a9247873b3":"Every program on this site in this group, with the schools each one serves. Pick a grade to narrow it down.","124a4fcef4":"Clubs a school runs for its own students aren’t in this list. They’re on that school’s page.","417e1c8db7":"Find your school.","fef0c0d418":"Other kinds of program","b101751332":"{type} clubs at the school itself","e3b6dc4c1d":"Run by a school for its own students, so they aren’t in the list above.","f4045b8b1d":"All {school} clubs","1b92377437":"Don’t see your school?","8a595d097a":"Every program, A to Z","ac075cc0b8":"All {n} after-school programs on this site, across every school. Narrow them by type, grade or neighborhood, then open one for its hours, cost and how to register.","ccb02c7cbf":"Find a program","5dc601f9f5":"To see only what works with your child’s school,","0bca0d8118":"start from your school.","1c1a8a8331":"Or see what’s close to home:","85f1c414ba":"browse by neighborhood.","83c87884b0":"Claimed","fbd282530b":"by the people who run it","839ac4f959":"The details","dc36c48813":"Add to your week","004aabe2fa":"Prices, hours and pickup routes change during the year. Confirm with the provider before you enroll.","85d2bc41a2":"Suggest an update","46ca4a8c8e":"Run this program?","acfbcd1618":"Claim this listing","b9d19eb873":"Tell me when sign-ups open","37251b2a49":"One email when {program} posts a sign-up date, a deadline or a day-off camp. Just this program. For every program at your school, sign up on your school’s page.","681d6aff8e":"Tell me","6c3e690795":"Only when this program posts something new, on a {day} morning. Every email has an unsubscribe link.","af2dbd1483":"Which schools it works for","cc668565fb":"Does it serve a school that isn’t shown here?","f0de56f174":"Tell us.","1337e21fd4":"What parents say","b9d6d369f7":"No reviews yet. If your child has been, a few sentences help the next family choose.","5346b4b0e7":"Write the first review","b50d68970d":"Reviews are first-hand notes from parents and caregivers. Each one is read before it’s posted.","4bab2d8fe1":"More","526cb7425a":"Less","fece5cf75f":"This year’s clubs","7491b76a4a":"From the school’s own list. Days, grades and openings change, so check with the club’s teacher before you count on one.","441d647554":"Day camps and weekend classes","9f35e0979c":"See its camp days","eb98694b26":"See its weekend classes","cdfb22c97e":"Listed for its day camps and weekend classes","1b5f5629de":"We couldn’t find a weekday after-school program here, so it isn’t on any school’s page.","a684b86420":"It runs camps on days school is closed, and children from any school can go.","71932aee10":"See its camp days.","6b88d1dc2a":"It runs classes on weekends.","a571f01a66":"See its weekend classes.","0ba4252490":"Does it run something after school that we missed?","07a857b5ac":"Weekends only","9e38e0e189":"Listed for its weekend classes","194e241b1b":"Day camps only","d7223a112b":"Listed for its day camps","e30e2ee39e":"We’ve only read up on its weekend classes so far, so it isn’t on any school’s page.","587c8b4e59":"After school, by neighborhood","8f3d592f5f":"Start from where you live. Each neighborhood lists the schools there and the programs based there, plus the ones that come to pick up.","1a4b3e864c":"A program is listed where its building is. Many pick up from schools in other neighborhoods, so your school’s page is still the fullest list.","c90125477b":"Don’t see your neighborhood?","07ede3f675":"Tell us which school or program to add.","d09357da10":"Weekend classes, by part of the city","b8d4acdd17":"Saturday and Sunday classes aren’t tied to a school, so they’re listed by where they are.","40e69b8340":"After school in {name}","266ac918e1":"The schools in {name}, the after-school programs based there, and the ones that come to pick up.","bbb2092610":"Schools in {name}","1e419c3218":"Programs based in {name}","c5fc322f8c":"Each one shows the schools it serves. Open it for hours, cost and how to register.","bc2cbd42ce":"Based elsewhere, but they pick up here","59e4b197e5":"These programs are in another neighborhood and collect children from a school in {name}.","ac59be7f27":"Weekend classes in {name}","3cb37ac44e":"Saturday and Sunday classes go by where they are. Any child can sign up, whichever school they go to.","0631b58248":"Close by, in {area}","9714dc4d38":"All weekend classes in {area}","32441257e2":"Other neighborhoods","d861b1fb98":"Weekend classes near {name}","dac2a8fa8c":"No school in {name} is on the site yet.","cb175bd67a":"Ask for yours.","06ac834ec6":"I’m {name}. I built this because sorting out after-school care for my own kid was chaos. If it saved you an evening of open tabs, a coffee is a nice way to say so.","767050dc15":"It goes to me, the person who built and updates this, for the hours spent checking listings and adding schools.","5c81cff8a1":"It’s a thank-you, not a charitable donation, so it isn’t tax-deductible.","54559419a5":"It buys nothing on the site. Listings are free for every provider, and nobody pays to be listed or to be listed higher.","599831ebe7":"Not a coffee person? A correction or a missing program helps just as much.","6d85a0da52":"Send one here.","3da90473e4":"Privacy, in plain English","adcf19af19":"This site is run by one parent. It collects as little as it can. Here is what it does collect, where it goes, and how to have it removed.","f7dd5c66e9":"The short version","a5fc51381d":"There are no ads, and nothing you send is sold. An account is optional: it is for keeping your school or a week in a profile, and for sharing a week with someone.","3b888bbdc0":"Your rosters, including any child’s name you type, are saved in your own browser. They are not sent to us unless you sign in and choose to keep one in your profile or share one.","66b0cd85db":"If you send a suggestion or a review, it arrives as an email to the person who runs the site.","ed9ee7d193":"If you ask for dates by email, your first name, your email address and the school or program you picked are kept by Klaviyo, the service that sends the emails.","664e73ba2e":"If you ask to be emailed when a school is added, the same three things are kept by Klaviyo: your first name, your email address and which school you’re waiting for. It also adds you to our email list for occasional news about the site.","f844260e06":"We use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to see how the site is used, so we can fix what’s confusing.","63e8b54c61":"Rosters and children’s names","5c228fe5c0":"A roster lives in the browser you made it in. Clearing your browser’s site data deletes it.","1f41fda416":"A summer schedule is kept the same way: the camps you picked for each week, and any first name you type, stay in your browser and are not sent to us unless you sign in and choose to keep the summer in your profile. A photo you add to a calendar picture is used once, in your browser, and is never saved or uploaded.","b7dac40b19":"If you save a school as yours, that choice is kept in your own browser too. Our visit counts record that a school was saved, not who saved it.","1253e5b11d":"A child’s name is optional. If you add one, it stays on your device unless you keep or share that week through an account.","72d228d3ed":"A week can no longer be shared as a link. A link showed the week to anyone who had it and could not be taken back, so links made before October 2026 have stopped opening.","2d3a826155":"If one of those older links is opened, the site still removes the name from the page address before any analytics loads. The roster page is set to be hidden in session recordings.","82b70f14b8":"Making a card happens on your own device. What you do with the picture is up to you.","2e3b852749":"If you add a photo to a week card, the card is made in your own browser. The photo is not uploaded, not saved, and gone when you close the page.","069e85c867":"Accounts, profiles and sharing","ea76bf36e5":"An account is optional. It lets you keep your school and a child’s week in a profile, share a week with one person, and join a share group of a few families who know each other. These are the only parts of the site that keep anything about a child on our server, and only when you choose to use them.","ec48d4711a":"An account is an email address and your first and last name. The email signs you in and tells you when someone opens a week you shared or joins a group you made. Other members never see it.","72a0cd17f3":"You can sign in with Google instead of an emailed code. Google’s button is loaded on the pages where you sign in, so Google can see that someone opened that page. If you use it, Google tells us your name and email address. We ask for nothing else and never see your Google password.","95462843af":"If you keep your school in your profile, we store which school. If you keep your children’s grades, we store the grades and nothing about which child is in which. If you keep a week in your profile, we store the child’s first name, the programs on their current and upcoming weeks, and the school each program was picked under, so the week can be put back on another device. Notes you type are not stored.","157bbafc71":"If you keep a summer schedule in your profile, we store each child’s first name as you typed it and the camps picked for each week, so the summer is there on your other devices. Ages, the calendar’s title and photos are not stored. A summer in your profile can’t be shared with anyone, and it is deleted when you take it out of your profile or delete your account. The summer schedule section is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is told only that a summer was kept, never what is in it.","ccbed3312d":"If you keep a days-off plan in your profile, we store each child’s first name as you typed it and the place picked for each day school is closed. The calendar’s title and photos are not stored. The plan can’t be shared with anyone, and it is deleted when you take it out of your profile or delete your account. The planner is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is never told what is in a plan you keep.","b97f9e1314":"Sharing a week with one person sends an invitation to the address you give. It only opens for someone signed in with that address, they can look and print but not change anything, and you can take it back at any time.","036b101d10":"Making an account also adds your name and email to our email list, kept by Klaviyo, for occasional news about the site. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing does not affect your account.","61b57a197b":"There are no passwords. We email you a link and a 6-digit code; each works once and for 15 minutes. A cookie then keeps that device signed in for 30 days, and you can sign out everywhere from your account page.","f04d299ecb":"When you add a week to a group, we store the child’s first name as you type it and the programs on their current and upcoming weeks. We do not store a last name, school, address, pickup time, note, teacher’s name, photo, price or day-off plan.","837ce2621f":"Nobody can find a group or ask to join one. The person who made it invites email addresses, and only someone signed in with an invited address, who also has the code from the invitation, gets in. A group isn’t listed anywhere, and its link shows nothing to anyone else.","32b6a5ac52":"If someone invites you, they give us your email address so we can send the invitation and recognise you if you join. We keep it with that group, use it for nothing else, and delete it when you are removed or the group ends. The invitation shows the name and email of the person who invited you.","0e7432357e":"A group’s creator sees the name and email address of each adult in it; other members don’t.","0a4f76533e":"Someone who joins to view only, such as a caregiver, can see and print the group and cannot change it.","dc603f7563":"Anyone in a group can print it or take a screenshot, so keep groups to people you know and would tell where your child is anyway.","3c2aef0577":"Accounts, profiles and groups are kept in a file on our web host, outside the public site. Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity are not loaded on your account page, on invitations or on group pages. Two pages around them do load them. The page where you create an account counts visits: its form is hidden in session recordings, and analytics is told only that a sign-up started, whether it used email or Google, and that it finished, never the address or a name. The Build your week page is hidden in session recordings too, and analytics is told only that something was kept or shared, never what or with whom.","fa3a27cb62":"We keep a daily count of how many accounts, shared weeks and groups were made, to see whether this is used. The counts hold no names, addresses or weeks.","a469bdc578":"You can take a week out of your profile or out of a group, stop sharing, leave a group, or delete your account from the site at any time, and it is removed straight away. A group’s creator can remove anyone. Every shared week and group is deleted two weeks after the last day of school.","35a4be5cea":"A safety copy of the accounts database is made each day and kept for 14 days, in case something breaks, and our web host keeps its own backups. So what you delete is gone from the site straight away, and leaves those copies as they are replaced, usually within a month.","4620ae226c":"Accounts are for parents, caregivers, teachers and the people who run programs. Children should not make one, and the site never asks a child for an email address: building a week and making a card work without an account.","de5ce68b78":"If you manage a program and claim its listing","3905d8d8ab":"Claiming uses the same account. We check one thing: that the email address you signed in with is at the listing’s own website address. We keep which listing you claimed, when, and whether the claim stands.","db601ebc70":"The public sees a “Claimed” mark on the listing and nothing about you. Your name and email address are seen only by the person who runs this site.","352fda9fb8":"Changes you propose are kept with your claim and emailed to the site’s inbox. They are checked and published by a person, and you are told by email when that happens.","550d83b376":"If you say whether there’s space, the listing shows “Spots open”, “Waitlist” or “Full” and the day you said it. It goes up at once, without anyone checking it, and comes down after 30 days unless you set it again.","4a55bb4633":"You can give up a claim at any time, and deleting your account removes your claims and the changes you proposed.","7d5d4993dc":"The page where you claim a listing loads Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to count visits. The part where you sign in and manage claims is hidden in session recordings.","7f8f847dc5":"Suggestions, corrections and reviews","6cc5cdc188":"What you type into a form is emailed to the site’s inbox, and a backup copy is kept on our web host in case the email goes missing.","94f7d60f5b":"Your email address is used only to reply to you or to confirm something. It is never published.","0e0b3194ab":"A review that is approved appears on the site with your first name, your child’s school and the month. Nothing else about you is shown.","73569b8eed":"Asking for a school to be covered sends only the school’s name.","b9fb0bfae2":"Please don’t include children’s names or other people’s personal details in what you send.","f9dda5e549":"Distances and the map","a81063878a":"“From where I am” asks your browser for your location. It is used on your device to work out distances, it is not sent to us, and it is not kept.","5320f4f2ab":"The map stays off until you tap “Show the map”. Its pictures then come from OpenStreetMap’s servers, which see your internet address and which part of the city you looked at, as any website you visit does.","be62daa255":"OpenStreetMap’s privacy policy","f8bbcf6d58":"Distances are measured in a straight line from street addresses, so a walk is usually a little longer.","9adee71854":"The sign-up form sends three things: your first name, your email address and the school or program you chose. They go from your browser to Klaviyo, the email service we use, and are stored there.","ec1764c464":"On a summer camp’s page the same form sends the camp you asked about, and you hear about that camp alone.","0f1b0b26a2":"It never asks for a child’s name, grade or anything else about your family, and your roster is not sent with it.","2542e24daf":"Klaviyo also notes which page you signed up on. Like most email services, it records whether an email was opened and which links were clicked, and it may estimate a general location from your internet connection.","1e3d45d7f9":"Your name and address are used for these date emails and nothing else. They are not shared with the programs listed here, and they are not sold.","3c33892438":"Every email has an unsubscribe link, and using it stops the emails. To have your name and address deleted altogether, email us.","02b6a17db4":"Klaviyo handles that data under its own terms:","a1f21c2fb6":"Klaviyo’s privacy notice","77a09c8b1d":"Analytics and recordings","44d34909fd":"Google Analytics records which pages are visited and which buttons, filters and searches are used, along with general details such as device type and approximate location. That includes the words typed into the program search box.","c4da07c2ab":"Microsoft Clarity records how pages are used, including heatmaps and replays of scrolling and clicking, to help us improve the site. We have set it to hide form fields and the roster page.","5811b84db9":"Both services use cookies and similar technologies, and Google and Microsoft handle that data under their own privacy terms:","04cb347cfe":"how Google uses information from sites that use its services","664944bb97":"the Microsoft Privacy Statement","6f46e689e8":"You can block both with your browser’s privacy settings or a content blocker, and the site will still work.","abba3c955f":"Like every website, our host keeps standard server logs, which include IP addresses.","bf541a9940":"Links to other sites","79d870e145":"Program websites, registration pages, calendars and Venmo are run by other organizations and have their own privacy practices.","d6a9374e67":"Links to a program’s own site carry a short tag saying the visit came from {site}, and from which school’s page. The tag says nothing about you.","dcf75191c5":"Children","5677caacfb":"This site is written for parents and caregivers. It is not meant to be used by children, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.","e9d0974c5f":"Seeing or removing what you sent","39a1146667":"To have a review taken down, your email address removed from the date emails, or a suggestion and your contact details deleted, email","30beaab727":". Say what you sent and roughly when, and it will be removed.","b149e0bbf0":"Last updated {date}. If this page changes in a way that matters, the date changes with it.","183f016fc2":"The rules for using this site, in plain English. Using the site means you agree to them.","a0ab6ffd0e":"What this site is","51a6b83435":"{site} is a free directory. It gathers what after-school programs, weekend classes and camps in Philadelphia say about themselves on their own websites, and arranges it by school and neighborhood.","3359d937ed":"We don’t run any of the programs listed, and we aren’t a child care provider, a school, a booking service or an agent for any program.","a45f772f57":"A listing is not a recommendation. We don’t inspect programs, check licences or insurance, run background checks on staff, or verify that a program is safe or right for your child.","ccb31de7db":"Hours, prices, dates, pickup routes and openings change, and what’s here can be out of date or wrong. Confirm everything with the program before you enroll, pay or rely on a pickup.","5c3a3567e1":"Choosing a program, and arranging how your child gets there and home, is your decision and your responsibility.","127d997818":"Who can use it","7a87c2d540":"The site is for adults: parents, guardians, caregivers and the people who run programs. Accounts are for people 18 and over. Children should not make an account or send us anything.","6f8cecd6f7":"If you make an account, use your own email address and your real name, and keep access to that email to yourself. You are responsible for what’s done from your account.","a8cc41044a":"Children’s information","56f90ab3bb":"The site works without telling us anything about a child. If you choose to keep a week or a summer in your profile, or share a week, you decide what first name to use, and you can use a nickname or an initial.","0d85524c8e":"Only add a child you are the parent or guardian of, or have that person’s permission to add.","e86e60b5ce":"What we store, and how to delete it, is on the privacy page.","15acae6ff2":"Read the privacy page.","9531476199":"Sharing a week, and groups","d406914b77":"When you share a week or start a group, you choose who sees it. We send the invitation to the email address you give and check that the person signs in with that address. We don’t know who they are beyond that, and we don’t screen anyone.","1e2c1717ca":"Only invite people you know and would tell where your child is anyway. Anyone you invite can print or screenshot what they see.","6e74d43811":"What happens between you and other people you meet or connect with through the site is between you and them. That includes carpools, shared pickups, playdates, babysitting and money. We are not a party to those arrangements and are not responsible for them.","d812cc1988":"You can stop sharing, leave a group or delete your account at any time.","0fa32ace54":"Reviews, suggestions and corrections","dc76296211":"A review should be your own first-hand experience, honest, and about the program rather than a named person. Don’t include children’s names or anyone’s private details.","30cf27f5e1":"We read reviews before they are posted, and we may shorten one, decline it or take it down. A review is the opinion of the person who wrote it, not ours.","b79a1e6de0":"By sending a review, suggestion or correction you let us publish it on the site and use it to improve the listings. You keep the rights to what you wrote.","fc4343257d":"If you run a program","a204462fcf":"Listings are free. We build them from your public website, and you can ask us to correct or remove one at any time.","c0616d13bf":"Claim a listing only if you work for that program and are allowed to speak for it. What you send us about it must be accurate and yours to share.","9d4227a64a":"Changes you propose are read before they go on the site. We may edit them to fit the page, decline them, or remove a claim.","ebff6cfde3":"A listing doesn’t make us your partner, agent or advertiser, and we don’t promise it will bring enrollments.","1d6ae60b32":"What’s not allowed","dd6ba10970":"Don’t use the site to harass anyone, to pretend to be someone else, or to collect information about children or families.","eb2fd2d272":"Don’t copy the listings in bulk to republish or sell them, and don’t try to break, overload or get around the site’s protections.","0ca4da443f":"We can suspend an account or remove content that breaks these rules.","08ad01556f":"Links and other services","dd480ef7a2":"The site links to programs’ own websites and sign-up pages. Those are theirs: their terms, prices and privacy practices apply there, and anything you buy or sign is between you and them.","d3ea60feaa":"Program names and logos belong to their owners. The rest of the site, including how the listings are written and arranged, is ours. You’re welcome to link to any page and to share the cards and calendars you make.","0bf64a9ab3":"No guarantees, and limits on our responsibility","19e569432c":"The site is provided as it is, free of charge, without any promise that it is complete, accurate, available or free of errors.","fc69e6d047":"As far as the law allows, {who} is not liable for loss or harm that comes from using the site, from relying on a listing, from a program you chose, or from your dealings with other people who use the site.","b4ec815cd0":"Nothing here limits any right you have that the law doesn’t allow to be limited.","f34c6e92f6":"Changes, and how to reach us","46a3253764":"We may change the site or these terms. When the terms change in a way that matters, the date below changes with them. If you keep using the site after that, the new terms apply.","a0c6aa03e7":"These terms are governed by the laws of Pennsylvania.","b112525712":"Questions about any of this:","83cf17eadd":"Last updated {date}.","d34fd34411":"One place to see what’s possible after the last bell","f6cc4005b7":"Finding after-school care means checking a dozen websites to learn who picks up from your school, for which grades, until when. {site} puts that on one page per school.","eb164ad365":"Each listing comes from the provider’s own public pages, the school’s site, or city program data. The sources are linked on every card.","3538dbc094":"Every card shows the date it was last checked. When a detail could not be confirmed, the card says so in a yellow note.","168197886b":"A program is marked “picks up” only when a source names the school. Otherwise it is listed as nearby.","e6927cf2fc":"What this site can’t promise","339b87f81a":"A listing is not an endorsement, and nobody pays to appear here.","02366fc9d1":"Prices, hours, openings and pickup routes change during the year. Confirm with the provider before you enroll.","116a91ada2":"{site} is independent. It is not affiliated with the School District of Philadelphia or any provider.","eb84427331":"Corrections, new programs and new schools","ba49970512":"Parents and providers know these programs best. If something is wrong or missing, or you want your school added,","67b96d067d":"use the form","6802c83437":"It helps to include the program, the school, what changed, and a link to where it’s published.","b83c4cdafe":"Reviews","5016c0caf6":"Reviews are first-hand notes from parents and caregivers. Each one is read before it’s posted and shows the reviewer’s first name and school.","98f6814b72":"We don’t post reviews that name children or individual staff, or reviews a program writes about itself.","db5ef27989":"Nobody pays to have a review posted or removed. A provider who thinks a review is wrong can use the form above or the contact address.","b96da3e11a":"Know one we missed?","3625d54ad4":"Plenty of good programs are off the radar: a church basement, a dance studio that walks kids over, a summer camp nobody has listed. Tell us and we’ll check it and add it. You can also send an update to a listing or ask for your school.","7c2fa947f6":"What are you sending?","06a83f5cdf":"The neighborhood helps too, if you know it.","6c52a3d661":"Which school?","1d2a2ff758":"For another school, name it in the details.","6200bb936f":"What kind of camp?","61acb05fb4":"Does it pick up from the school?","5c4698b6e0":"About you","d3f3c1b887":"All optional. Your email is only used to ask a follow-up question about what you sent.","b687c2eb73":"How we handle it.","f175d577f0":"How do you know it?","ab42293e29":"Your name","c4a3b42095":"Send it","51ecc5b21f":"What happens next","28af69d2cd":"Your note lands in a real inbox. A person reads it.","e836e8414a":"We check it against the program’s own information.","4a6923b699":"If it holds up, it goes on the site with its source and the date.","9fce963f8e":"Nothing is published automatically, and nobody pays to be listed.","41ace7cd55":"Run the program yourself?","fded9d2abb":"Claim your listing with your work email and send changes as its manager.","ee9ab1a21f":"How claiming works","815ecd6d02":"Got it. Thank you.","b3777a47d8":"We’ll check it against the program’s own information and add it if it holds up.","10b494ae4f":"Back to the schools.","7a304f2967":"What should this site do next?","ece8c308ad":"A missing filter, something confusing, a thing you wish it did. One person builds this, and reads every one.","fbcc6b1a22":"Your idea","93c7452449":"What were you trying to do, and what would have made it easier?","32861acdae":"Your name (optional)","41882a4420":"Your email (optional)","2b9e323f35":"Only used to ask a follow-up question.","5aa549ca95":"Send the idea","2f86a867fa":"Other things you can send","e6595d151a":"A program that’s missing, or a correction","a5839cf3a1":"A school you want covered","7253574d81":"A review of a program your child went to","5bbf44b373":"Ideas get read, and the ones that help the most families get built first.","21bec4e65a":"Back to the start.","c49bb4c242":"Get in touch","3801bea586":"A question, a problem with the site, something for the press, or just hello. This goes to the parent who runs the site.","19aad2a493":"So we can write back. It’s used for nothing else.","49d97c7a8e":"What’s it about?","f190c98ece":"Your message","dd705eff4c":"Other ways","84add5b295":"Email","ec4e916f64":"A program or camp that’s missing, or a listing that’s wrong:","52e582dc06":"use the suggestion form","f240b9c8ed":", so it reaches the right pile.","36bf5af840":"An idea for the site:","edfe97bc23":"request a feature","3efdf3b227":"You run a program:","27c911bccd":"claim your listing","4a5bb991f2":"One parent reads these, usually within a few days.","0c5a112d4f":"How we handle what you send.","b3d4ce50d0":"Sent. Thank you.","da79c88a05":"Your message is in the inbox. You’ll hear back by email, usually within a few days.","82a8bb5146":"Build your week","b8b650bf6a":"Monday might be martial arts and Thursday the rec center. Plan the term that’s coming, keep a second roster for what your child is doing now, and send either to your partner, a sitter, or the group chat. More than one child? Each gets their own.","7bf39f5748":"The roster needs JavaScript turned on.","6058b0c1c4":"That link doesn’t open a week any more","a394925693":"Weeks used to be shared as a link that anyone could open. They aren’t now. Ask the person who sent it to share the week with your email address instead: you’ll get an invitation, and it will open once you sign in.","0833e5be5f":"Child’s name","cdd763fac9":"Optional. It shows on the roster you share.","ae826cd301":"Roll a themed week","581db2b0e9":"Pick a school and a theme, and we’ll fill Monday to Friday.","f2f3d66a79":"School","aecc49c153":"Grade","044cf1802b":"Optional. It skips programs that don’t take that grade.","1427b5e649":"Music Prodigy","c90aa2dfa6":"Music every day","86a5a74e84":"Mathlete","1dc0fe5012":"STEM, chess and homework help","7fa36d2ec9":"The Da Vinci","e597bfefbd":"Art, science and music","25eb2ddb65":"Move It or Lose It","d4b2f6138c":"On their feet all week","5996e63410":"Glitter and Glue","3db3056781":"Arts and crafts all week","6d7fc1d86e":"Bookworm","ee18507fe8":"Reading, writing and the library","c983e0a563":"Just for Fun","5eddf4e50b":"Games, play and rec time","aef69a3a46":"Wild Child","1ba73b8295":"Outside whenever possible","90bb48964e":"Jack of All Trades","d2534fc212":"Something different every day","571059a6c2":"A themed week is a starting point, picked at random from what’s listed for that school. Check days, ages and open spots with each program before you plan around it.","6209822bd5":"Drag a card by its colored top to move it to another day, or use the day buttons on the card.","35a6da7355":"Looks right? Make it a picture.","637080ff4f":"One card of the week to text to your partner, stick on the fridge or hand to a teacher.","8fd63544b7":"Share this schedule","32f0ed93d5":"What this roster costs","5b53065afb":"An estimate from each program’s published prices, for half a school year: 18 weeks of school, or five monthly bills. It leaves out registration fees, deposits, materials, sibling discounts, subsidies and financial aid. If you know what you’ll pay, add it to any line; it stays on this device. Confirm the price with each program before you budget on it.","743e0828a8":"Plan the days off too","7efefe9180":"Want next term’s sign-up dates before they open?","d63b67808e":"Get the dates by email.","14ec1581e9":"Make it a card","ac085f0036":"One picture of the week to text, print, or hand to your child’s teacher, so they know where your child goes each day and who they are.","9c7696a8cb":"Who it’s for (optional)","a18fea4713":"A note (optional)","817e907c3b":"Your child’s photo (optional)","d03e72f9c9":"The photo never leaves this device. The card is made here in your browser, nothing is uploaded, and the photo isn’t saved.","ee82685bf6":"To email it to a teacher, share or save the card, then attach it to a message from your own email.","d5fe0a8fd9":"Want to keep this week too?","3a2b7f3ef2":"Save it to a free account so it’s on your phone and your computer, or share it with someone who signs in to see it.","121f62140c":"Save or share this week","58c9312de6":"School’s closed. Now what?","9cf234ddeb":"Every day district schools are closed this year, who runs a camp on each, and a plan you can build for each child.","997f30f482":"Your days off","916a9255ae":"Choose where each child will be on each day school is closed. Your picks are saved on this device and nowhere else.","cf3f7d3d6c":"First name (optional)","07620abf1b":"Stays on this device.","93a713d780":"Make it a calendar","1c38cce747":"One picture of every day off, or a calendar for each month, to print for the fridge or send to a sitter. Every child with a day planned is on it.","768e0c1c69":"Title","43381a8514":"A photo (optional)","25ff2a2f1c":"The photo never leaves this device. The calendar is made here in your browser, nothing is uploaded, and the photo isn’t saved.","8f95be3b1e":"Who’s open each day off","fa141c259e":"Each column is a day district schools are closed. A filled box means the program’s own site lists a camp that day. The chart scrolls sideways.","3256dd3f29":"Tap a box to put that day in your plan.","10f50270e6":"Camp posted","2b9e7b7ed1":"In your plan","a4fb91275c":"No dates posted yet","99f5031a01":"These programs say they run on days off but had no dates on their sites when we checked. You can still put one on any day above, then ask whether it’s open.","a1f2933bbb":"Days off still to come","28eb0e1ebe":"These are the School District of Philadelphia’s dates. A program is counted only when its own site lists that date.","1020a742a1":"Get a heads-up before each day off","aabd851130":"An email at least {n} days ahead, with the listed programs running a camp that day.","8422b24994":"Who runs something when school is closed","1d1ebf179a":"{n} listed programs say they run camps or full days on days off. {m} of them had no dates on their site when we checked, so ask which days they cover.","5266119c26":"Before you count on it","b9eff86fb0":"Expect to drop your child off. Several programs say there is no school pickup on a day school is closed.","939ba83ac9":"A camp day is usually booked and paid for on its own, separate from after-school.","23f3e9d859":"The district’s calendar lists no early-dismissal days for students this year. If your school sends children home early, ask the program what it does.","25eceb785b":"Charter schools keep their own calendars, so their days off can differ from these.","bc3d3a20ad":"Know a program that runs on days off and isn’t here?","a005b40584":"Full details","44e91e5e1f":"Summer camps in Philadelphia","1340bb3f65":"Day camps inside the city, with the ages, weeks, hours and prices each camp posts on its own site.","a306f0d8b7":"Most of what’s here is from summer {year}, shown as a guide.","2231b0eb6b":"Camps usually post next summer between December and March. Each listing changes to {year} when its camp posts dates and prices, and says so on its card.","6c10526de4":"Waiting on one camp? Its page has a box to be emailed when it posts.","94cd12d67e":"Plan your summer, week by week","5101f6a93d":"Looking for a particular camp?","26e0ca0aa1":"Grades here are worked out from each camp’s ages, so check the ages on the camp’s page. Each camp has its own page with everything it posts.","d8a720ac98":"Camps we haven’t been able to read yet","e65614e566":"These run day camps in the city too. Their details go up once we’ve read them on the camp’s own site.","028d1e3e42":"Suggest a camp","72ab82a2ab":"Know a city day camp that isn’t here? Send its name and its website, and we’ll read it and add it.","3ba73d32cf":"I run a camp","743141e3ff":"Listings come from each camp’s public pages and are not endorsements. Dates, prices and openings change, so confirm with the camp before you plan around it.","5be9f88d55":"These are its summer {year} details, shown as a guide.","0b1cec42d2":"It hasn’t posted summer {next} yet. This page changes when it does.","22c223a498":"Get an email when it does.","b2a7c8ed6e":"Weeks it ran in {year}","21de230914":"Each box is a week, named by its Monday in {year}: last summer’s weeks, moved to the same week of the calendar.","df3bcc82c1":"The camp’s website","b832b36463":"Add to your summer","45bac8d4ed":"Its school-year listing","06cc5e1c8d":"Dates, prices and openings change, and many camps fill early. Confirm with the camp before you plan around a week.","3979b00c23":"Run this camp?","294cd4499c":"Tell me when it posts summer {year}","a6df3cc4f0":"One email when {camp} posts its {year} dates and prices, and one before sign-ups open if it names a day. Just this camp.","fa74d98172":"Only about this camp, on a {day} morning. We read each camp’s site again about once a month, so the email can come a few weeks after the camp’s own announcement. If a camp fills fast, watch its site too. Every email has an unsubscribe link.","67d32633d0":"Camps close to this one","a464b2ae90":"It hasn’t listed dates we can chart.","48bdbd1d28":"Find or book a spot","6b7cb8066c":"Weeks it runs in {year}","36f240972c":"Each box is a week, named by its Monday.","8e1551a650":"Tell me when something changes","4f00f20960":"One email before sign-ups open at {camp}, if it names a day, and one when its dates or prices change. Just this camp.","bf38cb71fc":"{n} weeks between the last day of school and Labor Day. See which camps run each week, and line up your own summer.","2630f3292e":"Most of these dates are from summer {year}, shown as a guide.","8bcce75ac4":"A camp that hasn’t posted {next} yet is shown on the weeks it ran last summer, moved to the same week of the calendar. Camps usually post between December and March, and each one switches to its real dates when it does.","20c7d1ed6f":"Your summer","17b4a0ad84":"Add a camp to each week, for one child or for each of them. Your picks are saved on this device and nowhere else.","1464c87cf3":"Age this summer (optional)","07f65ead39":"One picture of the whole summer, or a calendar for each month, to print for the fridge or send to family. Every child with a camp picked is on it.","f87a087dc7":"When each camp runs","cf5610a79d":"Each column is a week, named by its Monday. A filled box means the camp listed that week. The chart scrolls sideways and down.","e615da79f1":"Tap a box to add that week to your summer.","b387b496c0":"{year} dates","3303fccc81":"{year} dates, as a guide","f1473f7521":"In your summer","c5a4c226c5":"No dates listed yet","219ba40bfa":"These camps haven’t put dates we can chart on their sites. You can still add one to any week above, then check with the camp.","0930275c37":"Every camp, with ages, hours and prices","9264c1c2d3":"Saturday and Sunday classes","b977f97057":"Weekend classes for kids, by part of the city: what runs, which term, and what it costs.","ea126e4246":"Looking for a particular class?","bfd62374ec":"A weekend class has no school pickup, so this list goes by where the class is. Any child can sign up, whichever school they go to.","fa6409c2a5":"This covers the programs already on this site, plus weekend-only places from a first sweep of the city. It isn’t every class in Philadelphia, and some listed programs run weekend classes that their sites don’t spell out by day, so ask.","363c044f46":"Know a weekend class that should be here?","e2bbe26a8b":"Weekend terms start and fill on their own dates, so check with the provider before you count on a class.","c32870d51a":"The dates, before they sneak up on you","98933ecbeb":"Sign-up openings, deadlines and days off for your school, by email. One short email on {day} morning, and nothing in a week with no dates.","77d81956df":"Where should they go?","aae5d56166":"Pick your school, then leave your first name and an email address. That’s the whole form.","ab11b57cad":"What you’ll get","dca1fbab07":"A heads-up when sign-ups open or a deadline is close at a program that serves your school.","3900e33c7c":"Each district day off at least {n} days ahead, with the listed programs running a camp that day.","17a60feb67":"One email a week at most. If your school isn’t listed yet, you get the days off and every listed program’s dates.","a6d743c0bb":"Waiting on one program? Each program’s page has a “Tell me when sign-ups open” box, for emails about that program alone.","fb894a5f1a":"Waiting on a summer camp? Each camp’s page has a box to be emailed when it posts next summer or names a sign-up day.","3225a10f0f":"No account, and no questions about your children.","ade5beae79":"Dates coming up","5607151fb2":"How did it go?","2ac3b3b289":"A first-hand note from one family helps the next one choose. Every review is read before it’s posted.","ce536c2876":"Which program?","68730f575a":"Your child’s school","83cd624d2e":"Your rating","501c17289a":"Your review","665f7e8d69":"What was pickup like? Homework help? Would you sign up again?","da1f043fb7":"Shown with your review.","2354db7577":"Never shown. Only used if we need to confirm something.","16add200f8":"This is my own experience as a parent or caregiver.","f4cfa14ce9":"Send review","48216a08c6":"House rules","568a415161":"First-hand only. Write about what your own family experienced.","1f0a3f8568":"Be specific and fair. Details help more than adjectives.","3f759500a1":"No names of children or individual staff.","21eeea0c1a":"Programs can’t review themselves.","8382938cc6":"Reviews show your first name and school, and appear after they’ve been read. Nobody pays to have a review posted or removed.","c35f6fbdee":"Thank you. It’s in.","65cb4c318e":"Your review will appear once it’s been read.","7a6310ea7e":"This jawn isn’t here","8e5ad16e04":"The link may be old, or the page moved.","8d980d5757":"Start from the list of schools.","94a8184560":"Log in to your account","7f010311e7":"Your school, your kids’ grades and your week, on any device. There’s no password to remember.","b81f2e17e0":"New here?","0701e850dd":"Keep your school and your child’s week in a profile, so they’re on every device you sign in on, and share a week with one person. Everything else on the site works without an account.","6efbd57efc":"Accounts need JavaScript turned on.","191885e234":"What an account gives you","b612bdccf0":"Save your school.","49dfeab767":"Every list starts from it, on any device you sign in on.","3a538b642b":"Save your kids’ grades.","c715faf072":"Lists open on the programs that take them.","24d8908789":"Keep your week.","19e77bcabf":"Build it on your phone tonight, find it on your laptop tomorrow.","d3a0950676":"Share a week with one person.","4523317b1d":"A grandparent or a sitter signs in to see it, and you can take it back.","31599229ab":"Share with a small group.","b7da72d2a0":"A few families you invite by email see each other’s weeks. Nobody else can find the group or ask to join.","fac03138c7":"It’s free. Nothing goes into your profile unless you put it there, and you can delete the account whenever you like.","6cb0c01f74":"Making an account means you agree to the","f137c5ff1a":"terms of use","89edaa0208":"Run a program or camp?","4b2b4e230b":". It’s the same account.","733d535919":"What an account keeps, and who sees it","bb4ca64d0e":"Nothing goes into your profile unless you put it there: a school, or a child’s first name and the programs on their week. No last names, addresses, notes or photos.","0dea7d9d59":"A shared week opens only for the email address you sent it to, once that person has signed in. It can’t be searched for, and its link shows nothing to anyone else.","d05870eaa7":"You can take a week back, stop sharing, or delete your account at any time. Shared weeks delete themselves when the school year ends.","2888e0b6c6":"The full details are on the privacy page.","d634af0382":"Create your free account","f1b7a0fc62":"Save your school, your kids’ grades and your week, and share a week with the people who need it. It takes about a minute, and there’s no password to remember.","6157136701":"Your group","390afd21ce":"Only the people invited to this group can see it.","1020e6eb49":"Groups need JavaScript turned on.","26dba34241":"Open your invitation","5db9909bea":"Someone shared a week with you or invited you to a group. Sign in with the email address the invitation was sent to: it only opens for that address.","5bf1f25f73":"Joining a group needs JavaScript turned on.","b0a8b36607":"What gets shared","64db7cc525":"A child’s first name and the programs on their week. No last names, addresses, notes or photos.","e94cfe6c62":"Only the people invited by email address can see it. Its link shows nothing to anyone else.","afbfa1f299":"If you add your own child’s week to a group, you can take it back out, leave the group or delete your account at any time.","6ff93ce468":"Run a program or camp? Claim your listing.","b4cef1b42e":"Find your program below and claim it with your work email. Then keep its dates, costs and hours up to date yourself. It’s free, and it takes a couple of minutes.","5cd372bd2a":"Claiming a listing needs JavaScript turned on.","237e65d7ff":"What claiming gets you","769128eff3":"Keep your dates current.","fe74e3dcea":"Post sign-up openings, deadlines, term dates and camp days as soon as you set them, instead of waiting for us to find them.","0624398afc":"Say whether there’s space.","2a7ed3b1a9":"Mark your listing “Spots open”, “Waitlist” or “Full”. It shows to parents straight away, with the date.","b5c01dd2e7":"Fix your costs and hours.","9f2ad635f9":"When a price or a pickup time changes, send it once and the listing follows.","59d55500b1":"Show parents it’s kept up.","6cef4c3b17":"A “Claimed” mark tells them the listing is looked after by the people who run it.","cbbfac7f02":"Find your listing.","1b5a2a50f1":"Search by name above. Every program and summer camp on the site is there.","bd5f48aa2a":"Sign in with your work email.","5a343478c1":"It has to be an address at your program’s own website: if the listing’s website is example.org, an address ending in @example.org. That is how we know you speak for it. If the addresses match, the claim stands straight away.","028587cbea":"Send changes when something moves.","0e10b31324":"New dates, a new price, new hours. We read each one and update the listing, usually within a few days.","79fc372dc7":"Good to know","1d92e2bf83":"A personal address (Gmail, Yahoo and so on) can’t claim a listing, even if it’s the one printed on your flyer. We have no way to tell it apart from anyone else’s.","301c1fb7c9":"“Continue with Google” works if your work email is a Google account at your program’s address. A personal Gmail account will sign you in, but it can’t claim anything.","df57559f10":"Some listings sit on a website many people share: a city rec center, a school’s clubs, a program inside a university. Those claims wait for us to say yes, and we may write to ask a question first.","83f5e887bb":"Parents see a “Claimed” mark on the listing. Your name and email address are never shown.","eeda369117":"A claim doesn’t change what the listing says by itself. Changes you send are looked at by a person, then published.","c44909adfd":"Listings are free and stay free. Nobody pays to be listed or to be ranked higher.","e09871422b":"Paid extras, such as a photo at the top of your listing, are planned for later.","114d2e3383":"Not on the site yet?","cb59876413":"Suggest your program","bcb356b14f":"your camp","bf7c4a20c3":", with its website, and claim it once it’s up.","31fedd6838":"What we keep about a claim is on the privacy page."}
